5.13.147.m:
He sets down the puroḍāśa to the north,
the groats to the south;
the parched grains remain in the receptacle itself.

5.14.147.m:
from the front half of the parched grains;
from the front half of the groats;
he bastes [them with butter];
he anoints [the cuts] in return;
having cut off [the portions] on the south side, he steps across to the north.

5.14.148.m:
He cuts off [a portion] from the middle of the parched grains;
from the middle of the groats;
from the middle of the puroḍāśa.

He bastes [them with butter];
he anoints [the cuts] in return;
having cut off [the portions] on the south side, he steps across to the north.

from the rear half of the puroḍāśa;
from the rear half of the parched grains;
he bastes [them with butter];

he anoints [the cuts] in return;
having cut off [the portions] on the south side, he steps across to the north;
he makes the call: "O svadhā!"

He bastes twice;
he does not anoint in return;
having cut off [the portions] on the south side, he steps across to the north.

These officiating priests exchange places;
they transpose the oblations;
he sets down the puroḍāśa to the south;
